{"status":"ok","message-type":"work","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,27]],"date-time":"2026-10-27T19:27:38Z","timestamp":1793129258725,"version":"4.5.0"},"reference-count":45,"publisher":"World Scientific Pub Co Pte Lt","issue":"02","content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["Open Syst. Inf. Dyn."],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2006,6]]},"abstract":"<jats:p> Complex Hadamard matrices, consisting of unimodular entries with arbitrary phases, play an important role in the theory of quantum information. We review basic properties of complex Hadamard matrices and present a catalogue of inequivalent cases known for the dimensions N = 2,\u2026,16. In particular, we explicitly write down some families of complex Hadamard matrices for N = 12, 14 and 16, which we could not find in the existing literature. <\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1007\/s11080-006-8220-2","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2006,5,19]],"date-time":"2006-05-19T12:03:13Z","timestamp":1148040193000},"page":"133-177","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":212,"title":["A Concise Guide to Complex Hadamard Matrices"],"prefix":"10.1142","volume":"13","author":[{"given":"Wojciech","family":"Tadej","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Faculty of Mathematics and Natural Sciences, Cardinal Stefan Wyszy\u0144ski University, Warsaw, Poland"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Karol","family":"\u017byczkowski","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Institute of Physics, Jagiellonian University, Krak\u00f3w, Poland"},{"name":"Center for Theoretical Physics, Polish Academy of Sciences, Warsaw, Poland"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"219","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2012,4,17]]},"reference":[{"key":"rf1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1080\/14786446708639914"},{"key":"rf2","first-page":"240","volume":"17","author":"Hadamard J.","journ